[2026-03-15T07:55:00.965Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FiE25m1V8yH7YX76Zu3rvX","type":"tool_result","content":"# replay-cli Reference\n\n**replay-cli** is a command-line tool for recording application sessions, gathering performance data, and debugging issues through Replay's platform.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\n1. Visit https://app.replay.io settings\n2. Create an API key\n3. Save it to the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** — Launch Replay Browser to record a session (defaults to `about:blank`)\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** — Upload recordings; opens interactive menu if no IDs provided\n- **`replayio list`** — Display all local recordings with status\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** — Delete recordings (use `-a` for all)\n- **`replayio login/logout`** — Manage account authentication\n- **`replayio info`** — Show CLI version and browser details\n\n## Common Workflow\n\nRecord a session and upload it:\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\nreplayio upload <recording-id>  # if not auto-prompted\n```\n\nFor detailed help on any command, use the `-h` or `--help` flag."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e0dc953-6a56-496e-90a1-1e4f359ead83","uuid":"9ffe684d-fc0b-4b57-a958-78b8eaddbde7","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# replay-cli Reference\n\n**replay-cli** is a command-line tool for recording application sessions, gathering performance data, and debugging issues through Replay's platform.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\n1. Visit https://app.replay.io settings\n2. Create an API key\n3. Save it to the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** — Launch Replay Browser to record a session (defaults to `about:blank`)\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** — Upload recordings; opens interactive menu if no IDs provided\n- **`replayio list`** — Display all local recordings with status\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** — Delete recordings (use `-a` for all)\n- **`replayio login/logout`** — Manage account authentication\n- **`replayio info`** — Show CLI version and browser details\n\n## Common Workflow\n\nRecord a session and upload it:\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\nreplayio upload <recording-id>  # if not auto-prompted\n```\n\nFor detailed help on any command, use the `-h` or `--help` flag.","durationMs":3728,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T07:55:01.470Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pvyvp5Nycye6nWqk2ZQyND","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution sessions. According to the documentation, \"Replay MCP is used to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\nThe tool provides three main categories of functionality:\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what happened during recording execution, including error detection, timeline analysis, and source code examination.\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred, using dependency tracking and detailed state inspection at specific execution points.\n\n**Investigative Approach**\n\nThe documentation emphasizes a structured methodology: frame questions clearly, use exploratory tools to identify relevant events, apply explanatory tools to understand causation, form hypotheses supported by data, and communicate conclusions with supporting evidence.\n\n## Important Concepts\n\nThe recording functions as \"essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed.\" Two foundational concepts are points (specific execution moments) and elements (DOM references independent of particular points).\n\nThe guidance suggests that \"when understanding JS behavior it is a good idea to find code relevant to the question being answered, see whether that code executed at all, and get details about the times when it executed.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e0dc953-6a56-496e-90a1-1e4f359ead83","uuid":"77c57848-23c8-424e-9025-79ba2bc5cf99","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution sessions. According to the documentation, \"Replay MCP is used to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\nThe tool provides three main categories of functionality:\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what happened during recording execution, including error detection, timeline analysis, and source code examination.\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred, using dependency tracking and detailed state inspection at specific execution points.\n\n**Investigative Approach**\n\nThe documentation emphasizes a structured methodology: frame questions clearly, use exploratory tools to identify relevant events, apply explanatory tools to understand causation, form hypotheses supported by data, and communicate conclusions with supporting evidence.\n\n## Important Concepts\n\nThe recording functions as \"essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed.\" Two foundational concepts are points (specific execution moments) and elements (DOM references independent of particular points).\n\nThe guidance suggests that \"when understanding JS behavior it is a good idea to find code relevant to the question being answered, see whether that code executed at all, and get details about the times when it executed.\"","durationMs":3373,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
